"The chapter describes a group of similar cells performing similar functions as a tissue. Different tissues are organised to form an organ, and several organs work together to form an organ system.",
"Follow the structure from small to large: cells with similar work form a tissue; different tissues make an organ; cooperating organs make an organ system. The respiratory system is the chapter's example, involving the nasal pores, nasal cavity, trachea and lungs. Higher levels of organisation do not replace the cell as the basic unit.",
